      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2017 AAGL. Published by Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Müllerian anomalies are anatomic disorders affecting the female reproductive tract, leading to a variety of physical symptoms, findings, and reproductive outcomes. Such anomalies are sufficiently common that most gynecologists will encounter women affected by them. Patients with obstructive müllerian anomalies generally present in adolescence with pain associated with the obstruction of menstrual outflow; thus, these disorders are frequently managed surgically. This review focuses on the surgical management of obstructive müllerian anomalies."
      },
